      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE",
          "content": "The purpose of this study is to test the reliability and validity of the 3-item Useful Depression Screening Tool (UDST) for use with older adults in congregate living settings."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "There were 176 residents of senior housing or assisted living who completed the UDST. Rasch analysis and test criterion relationships with pain, physical activity, and depression diagnosis were used to determine validity. Test-retest reliability was conducted with 29 senior housing residents."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Rasch analysis demonstrated good fit of all items to the concept of depression. Criterion validity was supported, F(5) = 14.17, p < .001. Test-retest showed no significant differences in UDST scores over time (p = .29)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "The findings provide support for the validity and reliability of the UDST for use with older adults in congregate living settings."
        }
      ]},
